#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
# Decides which issue an agent should pick up next, and why every other one is
# out. One definition of "eligible" rather than one per agent: the fleet only
# stays coherent if two agents waking up five seconds apart compute the same
# answer from the same board.
#
# next, why and settle deliberately do no network. Eligibility is a pure
# function of the issue set, and the fetch is the part that differs by surface.
# Making the caller supply the JSON keeps the part that would drift in one file
# and lets the part that varies stay varied.
#
# snapshot, claim and handoff are the GitHub fetch and write sequences around
# them, for a surface with `gh`. Every queue session used to hand-write these
# three, and the hand-written copies guessed settle's input keys wrong and lost
# a refspec to zsh's :r modifier. They call next and settle rather than
# repeating them, so the rules still live in one place.

usage() {
  cat <<'USAGE'
task-queue next [--queue <Ready|Needs review>] [--reviewer <identity>] [--runtime <cloud|local>] [--prefer <issue>] [--issues <file>] [--json]
task-queue why <issue> [--issues <file>] [--json]
task-queue settle --scenario <file> [--json]
task-queue validate-session --session <identity>
task-queue snapshot --profile <file> [--out <file>]
task-queue claim <issue> --profile <file> --session <identity> [--review] [--resume] [--out <file>]
task-queue handoff <issue> --pr <number>... --profile <file> --session <identity> --note-file <file> [--touches <paths>] [--out <file>]

GitHub sequences (a github-issues profile, gh, python3 and jq). Each prints one
verdict line ending in the path of a JSON file with the detail, written under
$TMPDIR unless --out names one. In Cursor Cloud (CURSOR_CLOUD_AGENT set) every
issue read and write carries GH_JCLAW_LABS_ISSUE_TOKEN with tracing off, and
fails before any traffic when it is unset; PR and ref traffic keeps the ambient
credential. claim-replay and issue-fields resolve from this file's directory,
then issue-fields from the checkout holding it (bin/), then PATH.

  snapshot  Lists open issues through issue-fields, maps open PRs (with their
            files) to owner issues, replays every Ready, In progress, Needs
            review and Under review issue through claim-replay, and runs next.
            A failed replay becomes that record's normalization_error. The
            verdict names the first eligible Ready issue whose visit replay
            says is claimable; eligible ones that are not are listed under
            unclaimable_ready. Review selection is not covered: it needs
            stack_ancestors, implementation_authors and runtime_target.
  claim     Requires Queue Ready (Needs review with --review) and a claimable
            replay, then posts the marker, writes Queue, posts claim-set and
            the Claim projection, re-reads, settles, converges Claim to the
            winner, and creates claude/issue-<n>-<generation>
            (claude/review-... with --review) from the default branch head,
            running the rejected-ref protocol on a 422, at most three times.
            When the refs API refuses otherwise, it pushes the ref create-only
            from the current directory if that is a checkout of the
            repository; only a push that creates the ref is a win, and any
            other accepted push is a rejection. Exit 0 on a win, 3 on a loss
            or an unclaimable visit, 4 when the claim is held but the ref
            could not be created. --resume skips the claim writes and retries
            the ref for a visit replay shows this session already holding.
  handoff   Requires Queue In progress and a replayed Claim naming --session
            in the active generation, and every --pr open and either owning
            the issue or stacked on or under one that does. Writes Touches
            when --touches is given (empty clears it), posts the note with
            the profile's prefix, the scoped claim-clear,
            the Needs review intent, the Queue write and the activation,
            clears the Claim projection, and verifies by replay that the new
            visit is claimable and unheld.

Reads a normalised issue set and reports the queue in pick order, or why one
issue is not pickable.

Input is a JSON array, from --issues, from TASK_QUEUE_ISSUES_FILE, or on stdin:

  [{ "number":   126,
     "title":    "...",
     "queue":    "Ready",
     "priority": "High",
     "claim":    "sess-9",
     "blocked_by": [134],
     "stack_ancestors": [120],
     "implementation_authors": ["worker-session"],
     "runtime_target": "either",
     "normalization_error": null,
     "touches":  ["apps/web/src/app/page.tsx"],
     "open_prs": [472],
     "context_only": false }]

The keys map to issue fields: queue is Queue, blocked_by is "Blocked by issue",
touches is Touches, priority is Priority, claim is Claim.
context_only marks an open blocker fetched only to close a scoped dependency
graph. It can block an in-scope issue but is never itself pickable.

"Blocked by issue" and Touches are single text fields, so SPLITTING THEM ON
WHITESPACE IS THE CALLER'S JOB: "134 96" becomes [134, 96], not ["134 96"].
Forgetting is the likeliest bug on this path, so an entry still carrying a space
is reported against its own issue rather than read past -- reading only the first
number in it used to hand out an issue whose other blocker was wide open.

What a person typed is read where it can be: a blocked_by entry gives up every
number in it, so "#134" is 134. An entry with no number in it holds its own issue
back and says so, because an unreadable blocker might be an open one. Only the
JSON shape is refused outright, and only a normaliser chooses that.

If one issue's claim replay or review authorship cannot be normalized safely,
set normalization_error to a nonempty diagnostic and preserve its Queue and
Touches. That record is ineligible, still holds files when its Queue is in
flight, and does not prevent a valid sibling from being selected. Do not invent
Claim, generation, ancestry, or authorship to fill the gap.

Pass every OPEN issue. A number under blocked_by that is absent from the input
is read as closed -- and reported as a warning, because a typo looks the same.

An issue is eligible when all three hold:
  - queue matches the selection target (Ready by default; Needs review for review work)
  - every blocked_by issue and stack ancestor is closed
  - its touches do not overlap any held by an issue in flight, where in flight
    means In progress, Needs review, Under review, or Ready to merge

For review selection, another issue waiting in Needs review holds no files:
a review nobody has claimed edits nothing, and each review commits only to its
own PR branch, so overlapping reviews collide at merge rather than in a shared
tree. A claimed review (Under review) still holds its files, and so does Ready
to merge.
Counting them made overlapping reviews lock each other with none pickable
(#679). In progress, Under review, and Ready to merge keep their locks, and so
does a Needs review record whose normalization failed, since its claim replay
may be hiding a live review.

stack_ancestors contains every owner issue below this issue in its live PR
stack. Its open ancestry keeps a descendant behind the bottom issue, so the
stack is still reviewed bottom-up. Every Needs-review record must carry stack_ancestors.
An explicit [] means the live graph proved that no unmerged owner ancestor
exists; an omitted field makes only that record ineligible. Malformed or cyclic
ancestry fails closed.

Every Needs-review record must also carry implementation_authors as a unique,
nonempty array of session tokens. A session token is nonempty and contains no
colon, ASCII whitespace, <, or >. The caller passes its token with --reviewer.
The executable derives
review_excluded by exact membership and ignores any caller-supplied field of
that name. Missing authorship makes that record ineligible. A normalizer that
cannot establish valid authorship uses normalization_error so only that record
is ineligible; a malformed implementation_authors value passed as normalized
input remains a document-shape error. An excluded record reports that
self-authored work cannot be reviewed; its unmerged branch holds every declared
file against implementation picks, but like any unclaimed review it holds
nothing against another review pick.

Every Needs-review record must also carry runtime_target: the runtime target
recorded in its implementation PR's agent context, as "cloud", "local",
"either", or "both", or null when the work is not agent-facing. The caller
names the runtime it reviews in with --runtime cloud or --runtime local. null
and "either" are certifiable from either runtime; "cloud" and "local" only from
that runtime; "both" from neither, because one reviewer checks one path. An
incompatible record is ineligible and says which runtime it needs, but stays in
flight: it holds its files against implementation picks, and like any
unclaimed review it holds nothing against another review pick. A missing runtime_target makes only that record
ineligible; any other value is a document-shape error.

open_prs lists the open pull requests that implement the issue: the caller maps
each open PR to its owner issue through a closing keyword (close, fix or
resolve in any tense or case, then #n) or a claude/issue-<n> or
claude/work-issue-<n> head branch with or without a -suffix. It is optional; an
omitted or empty field means no open PR is known, and the record is read exactly
as it was before the field existed. A Ready issue with an open PR stays
eligible, because claim-task's reclaim path returns an issue whose PR lost its
authorship to Ready so a worker can adopt it. It sorts after every eligible
Ready issue without one, its reason says to adopt or verify the PR rather than
implement again, and a warning reports it as a stewardship finding. Its branch
is live, so like a waiting review it holds its Touches against Ready picks that
have no open PR, but not against another Ready issue with one or against review
picks. An in-flight record that shares an open PR with a Ready record holds that
Ready pick whatever their Touches, so two workers are never sent to the same
branch; two Ready records that share a PR stay both pickable until one is
claimed. So in-flight records' open_prs matter too, and the caller fills them
for every record, not only Ready ones. Otherwise the field is Ready-only: review
selection reads Needs review and later records as before.

With --queue "Needs review", --prefer may name the next owner in a stack already
being reviewed. A fully eligible preferred record comes first even when another
eligible issue has higher Priority. If that record is blocked, locked, behind an
open ancestor, missing ancestry, or otherwise ineligible, selection falls back
to the canonical priority and issue-number order.

Every state from In progress onward holds its files, because the branch is
unmerged in all of them: a second agent branching off the default branch would
collide at merge rather than at pick time. Ready to merge holds them most
certainly of all -- the work is finished and waiting on a human.

Waiting for input is the other end of that sentence and its opposite in every
mechanical way: nothing has started, so there is no branch, so it holds no
files -- Triage and Ready are its neighbours there, not Ready to merge. Both it
and Ready to merge wait on a person; only one of them has work behind it.
Putting finished work here instead releases the files of a branch that is still
out there, which is the one way this state can do damage.

Queue is matched case-insensitively, so "In Progress" is that state rather than
a typo for it. A value outside the seven holds its files anyway and is reported,
because serialising work that could have run costs throughput while releasing a
lock by accident costs two agents editing the same file.

An in-flight issue that declares no touches holds nothing, and says so -- that
is a triage omission rather than a task with no files.

Ties break by priority (Urgent, High, Medium, Low), then issue number ascending.
An unset priority sorts last, so forgetting to set one cannot promote an issue.
A priority outside those four also sorts last and is reported as a warning,
because a scale nobody declared is not a scale.

Settlement scenarios carry the active claim generation, and every marker carries
the generation it read before claiming. Only markers from that generation enter
the tie; an older visit to the same held state cannot win a later cycle. Claim is
null or an authoritative event with value, held state, and generation. The lock
ref includes that generation, so later work and review cycles get fresh locks
while racers in one cycle still converge on one name.
USAGE
}

die() { echo "task-queue: $1" >&2; exit 1; }

session_token_regex='^[^:\x09-\x0D\x20<>]+$'

is_session_token() {
  local value="${1-}"
  [ -n "$value" ] || return 1
  case "$value" in
    *:*|*"<"*|*">"*|*" "*|*$'\t'*|*$'\n'*|*$'\r'*|*$'\f'*|*$'\v'*)
      return 1
      ;;
  esac
  return 0
}

require_session_token() {
  local value="$1" name="$2"
  is_session_token "$value" \
    || die "$name must be a session token: nonempty and without colon, ASCII whitespace, <, or >"
}

validate_unique_json() {
  local value="$1" error
  command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1 || die "python3 is required"
  if ! error="$(printf '%s' "$value" | python3 -c '
import json
import sys

class DuplicateKey(Exception):
    pass

def unique_object(pairs):
    result = {}
    for key, value in pairs:
        if key in result:
            raise DuplicateKey(key)
        result[key] = value
    return result

try:
    json.load(sys.stdin, object_pairs_hook=unique_object)
except DuplicateKey as error:
    print(f"duplicate JSON object key: {error.args[0]}")
    raise SystemExit(1)
except (json.JSONDecodeError, UnicodeDecodeError):
    print("input is not valid JSON")
    raise SystemExit(1)
')"; then
    die "${error:-input is not valid JSON}"
  fi
}

cmd="${1:-}"; shift 2>/dev/null || true
case "$cmd" in
  next|why|settle|validate-session|snapshot|claim|handoff) ;;
  -h|--help|"") usage; exit 0 ;;
  *) die "unknown command: $cmd (expected next, why, settle, validate-session, snapshot, claim, or handoff)" ;;
esac

if [ "$cmd" = validate-session ]; then
  session=""; session_given=0
  while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
    case "$1" in
      --session)
        [ $# -ge 2 ] || die "--session needs a value"
        [ "$session_given" = 0 ] || die "session may be provided only once"
        session="$2"; session_given=1; shift 2
        ;;
      -h|--help) usage; exit 0 ;;
      -*) die "unknown flag: $1" ;;
      *) die "unexpected argument: $1" ;;
    esac
  done
  [ "$session_given" = 1 ] || die "validate-session needs --session"
  require_session_token "$session" "session"
  exit 0
fi

# --- GitHub transport: snapshot, claim, handoff ------------------------------
# Everything above this block and below it is a pure function of its input.
# These three commands are the GitHub side every queue session used to write by
# hand: fetch, replay, post the markers, write the fields, settle, lock. Each
# one prints a one-line verdict and leaves the detail in a JSON file, so a
# session reads one line instead of the comment stream.
#
# Credential contract (steward-task-queue, Cursor Cloud): issue reads and writes
# carry GH_JCLAW_LABS_ISSUE_TOKEN with tracing off; PR and git-ref traffic stays
# on the ambient installation credential. Outside Cursor Cloud both use ambient
# gh auth. Siblings resolve from this file's own directory.

self_path() {
  python3 -c 'import os, sys; print(os.path.realpath(sys.argv[1]))' "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}"
}

gh_setup() {
  local profile_file="$1"
  command -v jq >/dev/null 2>&1 || die "jq is required"
  command -v gh >/dev/null 2>&1 || die "gh is required"
  command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1 || die "python3 is required"
  [ -n "$profile_file" ] || die "$cmd needs --profile"
  [ -r "$profile_file" ] || die "cannot read profile $profile_file"
  jq -e '.backend == "github-issues"' "$profile_file" >/dev/null 2>&1 \
    || die "$cmd needs a github-issues profile"
  repo="$(jq -er '.tracker.repository' "$profile_file")" || die "profile has no tracker.repository"
  api_version="$(jq -er '.tracker.api_version' "$profile_file")" || die "profile has no tracker.api_version"
  comment_prefix="$(jq -er '.writes.comment_prefix' "$profile_file")" || die "profile has no writes.comment_prefix"
  queue_field="$(jq -er '.tracker.fields.queue' "$profile_file")" || die "profile has no queue field"
  claim_field="$(jq -er '.tracker.fields.claim' "$profile_file")" || die "profile has no claim field"
  if [ -n "${CURSOR_CLOUD_AGENT:-}" ] && [ -z "${GH_JCLAW_LABS_ISSUE_TOKEN:-}" ]; then
    die "GH_JCLAW_LABS_ISSUE_TOKEN is required for GitHub queue traffic"
  fi

  self="$(self_path)"
  local here
  here="$(dirname "$self")"
  claim_replay="$here/claim-replay"
  [ -x "$claim_replay" ] || die "claim-replay is missing beside $self"
  # Bundled beside this file first, then the checkout that contains it (a
  # local-config source tree keeps it under bin/), then PATH.
  issue_fields="$here/issue-fields"
  if [ ! -x "$issue_fields" ]; then
    local top
    top="$(git -C "$here" rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null || true)"
    issue_fields="${top:+$top/bin/issue-fields}"
  fi
  if [ -z "$issue_fields" ] || [ ! -x "$issue_fields" ]; then
    issue_fields="$(command -v issue-fields 2>/dev/null || true)"
  fi
  [ -n "$issue_fields" ] && [ -x "$issue_fields" ] || die "issue-fields command is unavailable"

  scratch="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/task-queue.XXXXXX")" || die "cannot create a scratch directory"
  trap 'rm -rf "$scratch"' EXIT
}

issue_api() {
  { set +x; } 2>/dev/null
  if [ -n "${CURSOR_CLOUD_AGENT:-}" ]; then
    GH_TOKEN="$GH_JCLAW_LABS_ISSUE_TOKEN" gh api -H "X-GitHub-Api-Version: $api_version" "$@"
  else
    gh api -H "X-GitHub-Api-Version: $api_version" "$@"
  fi
}

run_issue_fields() {
  { set +x; } 2>/dev/null
  if [ -n "${CURSOR_CLOUD_AGENT:-}" ]; then
    GH_TOKEN="$GH_JCLAW_LABS_ISSUE_TOKEN" "$issue_fields" "$@"
  else
    "$issue_fields" "$@"
  fi
}

pr_api() { gh api "$@"; }

out_file() {
  local name="$1" given="$2"
  if [ -n "$given" ]; then
    : >"$given" || die "cannot write $given"
    printf '%s\n' "$given"
  else
    mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/task-queue-$name.XXXXXX" || die "cannot create an output file"
  fi
}

# The seven Queue values, matched case-insensitively as next does.
canon_queue() {
  jq -rn --arg q "$1" '
    ["Triage", "Waiting for input", "Ready", "In progress", "Needs review",
     "Under review", "Ready to merge"]
    | map(select(ascii_downcase == ($q | ascii_downcase))) | .[0] // ""'
}

# Prints {"queue": ..., "claim": ...} for one issue from its live field values.
read_fields() {
  issue_api "repos/$repo/issues/$1/issue-field-values" \
    | jq -ce --argjson q "$queue_field" --argjson c "$claim_field" '
        def val: if .data_type == "single_select" then .single_select_option.name else .value end;
        def field($id): (map(select(.issue_field_id == $id)) | .[0]) as $e
                        | if $e == null then null else ($e | val) end;
        if type != "array" then error("field values must be an array") else
          {queue: field($q), claim: field($c)} end' \
    || die "cannot read the fields of #$1"
}

# Writes the github-claim-comments-v1 replay input for one issue.
fetch_comments() {
  local issue="$1" projection="$2" dest="$3" page=1 count
  : >"$scratch/pages"
  while :; do
    issue_api "repos/$repo/issues/$issue/comments?per_page=100&page=$page" >"$scratch/page" \
      || return 1
    count="$(jq -e 'if type == "array" then length else error("not an array") end' "$scratch/page")" \
      || return 1
    cat "$scratch/page" >>"$scratch/pages"
    [ "$count" -lt 100 ] && break
    page=$((page + 1))
  done
  jq -s --arg p "$projection" '
    {format: "github-claim-comments-v1", claim_projection: $p,
     comments: [add // [] | .[]
                | {databaseId: .id, createdAt: .created_at,
                   updatedAt: .updated_at, body: .body}]}' \
    "$scratch/pages" >"$dest"
}

# replay <issue> <queue-state> <projection> <dest>; on failure the reason is in
# $scratch/replay-error.
replay_issue() {
  local issue="$1" state="$2" projection="$3" dest="$4"
  : >"$scratch/replay-error"
  if ! fetch_comments "$issue" "$projection" "$scratch/comments-$issue.json" 2>"$scratch/replay-error"; then
    printf 'cannot read the comments of #%s\n' "$issue" >>"$scratch/replay-error"
    return 1
  fi
  "$claim_replay" github --input "$scratch/comments-$issue.json" \
    --queue-state "$state" --comment-prefix "$comment_prefix" --json \
    >"$dest" 2>"$scratch/replay-error"
}

replay_error() {
  tr '\n' ' ' <"$scratch/replay-error" | sed 's/^claim-replay: //; s/ *$//'
}

post_comment() {
  issue_api --method POST "repos/$repo/issues/$1/comments" -f "body=$2" \
    | jq -er '.id' || die "cannot comment on #$1"
}

set_field() {
  run_issue_fields set --profile "$profile" --issue "$1" --value "$2" >/dev/null \
    || die "cannot set $2 on #$1"
}

clear_field() {
  run_issue_fields clear --profile "$profile" --issue "$1" --field "$2" >/dev/null \
    || die "cannot clear $2 on #$1"
}

# Owner issues an open PR implements: a closing keyword in its body, or a
# claude/issue-<n> or claude/work-issue-<n> head branch, with or without a -suffix.
pr_owners_jq='
  def owners:
    ([(.head.ref // "") | capture("^claude/(work-)?issue-(?<n>[0-9]+)(-|$)") | .n]
     + [(.body // "") | scan("(?i)\\b(?:close[sd]?|fix(?:e[sd])?|resolve[sd]?)[ \\t]+#([0-9]+)\\b") | .[0]])
    | map(tonumber) | unique;'

# --- snapshot -----------------------------------------------------------------
cmd_snapshot() {
  local out_given="" n state projection rc
  profile=""
  while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
    case "$1" in
      --profile) [ $# -ge 2 ] || die "--profile needs a value"; profile="$2"; shift 2 ;;
      --out) [ $# -ge 2 ] || die "--out needs a value"; out_given="$2"; shift 2 ;;
      -h|--help) usage; exit 0 ;;
      -*) die "unknown flag: $1" ;;
      *) die "unexpected argument: $1" ;;
    esac
  done
  gh_setup "$profile"
  local out
  out="$(out_file snapshot "$out_given")"

  run_issue_fields list --profile "$profile" >"$scratch/fields.json" \
    || die "cannot list the open issues"

  local page=1 count
  : >"$scratch/pr-pages"
  while :; do
    pr_api "repos/$repo/pulls?state=open&per_page=100&page=$page" >"$scratch/page" \
      || die "cannot list open pull requests"
    count="$(jq -e 'if type == "array" then length else error("not an array") end' "$scratch/page")" \
      || die "open pull requests page is not an array"
    cat "$scratch/page" >>"$scratch/pr-pages"
    [ "$count" -lt 100 ] && break
    page=$((page + 1))
  done
  jq -s "$pr_owners_jq"'
    [add // [] | .[] | {number, title, head: .head.ref, draft: (.draft // false), owners: owners}]' \
    "$scratch/pr-pages" >"$scratch/prs.json"

  printf '[]' >"$scratch/pr-files.json"
  for n in $(jq -r '.[].number' "$scratch/prs.json"); do
    page=1
    : >"$scratch/file-pages"
    while :; do
      pr_api "repos/$repo/pulls/$n/files?per_page=100&page=$page" >"$scratch/page" \
        || die "cannot list the files of PR #$n"
      count="$(jq -e 'if type == "array" then length else error("not an array") end' "$scratch/page")" \
        || die "files page of PR #$n is not an array"
      cat "$scratch/page" >>"$scratch/file-pages"
      [ "$count" -lt 100 ] && break
      page=$((page + 1))
    done
    jq -s --argjson n "$n" --slurpfile acc "$scratch/pr-files.json" \
      '$acc[0] + [{number: $n, files: [add // [] | .[].filename]}]' \
      "$scratch/file-pages" >"$scratch/pr-files.next"
    mv "$scratch/pr-files.next" "$scratch/pr-files.json"
  done
  jq --slurpfile files "$scratch/pr-files.json" '
    ($files[0] | map({key: (.number | tostring), value: .files}) | from_entries) as $f
    | map(. + {files: ($f[.number | tostring] // [])})' \
    "$scratch/prs.json" >"$scratch/prs-with-files.json"

  # Replay every issue in a claimable or held state. A record whose replay
  # fails keeps its Queue and Touches and becomes ineligible, as next expects.
  printf '{}' >"$scratch/replays.json"
  while IFS=$'\x1f' read -r n state projection; do
    state="$(canon_queue "$state")"
    case "$state" in
      Ready|"In progress"|"Needs review"|"Under review") ;;
      *) continue ;;
    esac
    if replay_issue "$n" "$state" "$projection" "$scratch/replay-$n.json"; then
      jq --arg n "$n" --arg s "$state" --slurpfile r "$scratch/replay-$n.json" \
        '. + {($n): ($r[0] | {queue_state: $s, claim, generation: (.generation.id // null),
                              transition, projection, error: null})}' \
        "$scratch/replays.json" >"$scratch/replays.next"
    else
      jq --arg n "$n" --arg s "$state" --arg e "$(replay_error)" \
        '. + {($n): {queue_state: $s, error: $e}}' \
        "$scratch/replays.json" >"$scratch/replays.next"
    fi
    mv "$scratch/replays.next" "$scratch/replays.json"
  done < <(jq -r '.[] | [(.number | tostring), (.queue // ""), (.claim // "")] | join("\u001f")' "$scratch/fields.json")

  jq --slurpfile prs "$scratch/prs.json" --slurpfile replays "$scratch/replays.json" '
    ($replays[0]) as $r
    | map(. as $i
          | ($r[$i.number | tostring]) as $rep
          | $i + {open_prs: [$prs[0][] | select(.owners | index($i.number)) | .number]}
          | if $rep == null then .
            elif $rep.error != null then . + {normalization_error: "claim replay failed: \($rep.error)"}
            else . + {claim: ($rep.claim.value // null)} end)' \
    "$scratch/fields.json" >"$scratch/issues.json"

  rc=0
  "$self" next --issues "$scratch/issues.json" --json >"$scratch/selection.json" 2>"$scratch/selection-error" || rc=$?
  [ "$rc" = 0 ] || die "next refused the snapshot: $(tr '\n' ' ' <"$scratch/selection-error")"

  jq -n --arg repo "$repo" --arg taken "$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)" \
    --slurpfile issues "$scratch/issues.json" \
    --slurpfile prs "$scratch/prs-with-files.json" \
    --slurpfile replays "$scratch/replays.json" \
    --slurpfile selection "$scratch/selection.json" '
    ($replays[0]) as $r
    | ($selection[0].queue
       | map(select(.eligible and .state == "Ready"
                    and (($r[.number | tostring].transition.claimable // false) | not)))
       | map({number, reason: ($r[.number | tostring]
                               | if .error != null then .error
                                 else (.transition.reason // .transition.status // "no replay") end)}))
      as $unclaimable
    | {format: "task-queue-snapshot-v1", repository: $repo, taken_at: $taken,
       next: ($selection[0].queue
              | map(select(.eligible and (.number as $n | $unclaimable | map(.number) | index($n) | not)))
              | .[0].number // null),
       unclaimable_ready: $unclaimable,
       selection: $selection[0],
       issues: $issues[0], pull_requests: $prs[0], replays: $r}' >"$out"

  jq -r --arg out "$out" '
    (.selection.queue | map(select(.eligible)) | length) as $pickable
    | (.selection.queue | map(select(.eligible | not)) | length) as $held
    | (.selection.queue | map(.warnings) | add // [] | unique | length) as $warnings
    | (.next) as $next
    | (if $next == null then "nothing claimable"
       else (.selection.queue[] | select(.number == $next)
             | "next #\(.number) (\(.priority // "unset")) \(.title)") end)
      + "; \($pickable) pickable, \($held) held back, \($warnings) warnings"
      + (if (.unclaimable_ready | length) > 0
         then ", \(.unclaimable_ready | length) eligible but not claimable" else "" end)
      + "; snapshot \($out)"' "$out"
}

# --- claim --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Re-reads the issue in its held state, settles, and converges Claim. Leaves
# the settlement in $scratch/settled.json and the replay in $scratch/held.json.
settle_fresh() {
  local issue="$1" held="$2" session="$3" fields live projection
  fields="$(read_fields "$issue")"
  live="$(canon_queue "$(jq -r '.queue // ""' <<<"$fields")")"
  [ "$live" = "$held" ] \
    || die "#$issue left $held during the claim (Queue is now ${live:-unset}); select again"
  projection="$(jq -r '.claim // ""' <<<"$fields")"
  replay_issue "$issue" "$held" "$projection" "$scratch/held.json" \
    || die "claim replay of #$issue failed: $(replay_error)"
  jq -e '.generation.id != null' "$scratch/held.json" >/dev/null \
    || die "#$issue has no active generation after the claim"
  jq -n --argjson issue "$issue" --arg caller "$session" --arg state "$held" \
    --arg now "$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)" --slurpfile r "$scratch/held.json" '
    {issue: $issue, caller: $caller, target_state: $state, claim: $r[0].claim,
     generation: $r[0].generation.id, now: $now, stale_after_seconds: 14400,
     markers: $r[0].markers}' >"$scratch/scenario.json"
  "$self" settle --scenario "$scratch/scenario.json" --json >"$scratch/settled.json" \
    2>"$scratch/settle-error" \
    || die "settlement of #$issue failed: $(tr '\n' ' ' <"$scratch/settle-error")"

  local value state generation
  if [ "$(jq -r '.write_claim' "$scratch/settled.json")" = true ]; then
    value="$(jq -r '.desired_claim_event.value' "$scratch/settled.json")"
    state="$(jq -r '.desired_claim_event.state' "$scratch/settled.json")"
    generation="$(jq -r '.desired_claim_event.generation' "$scratch/settled.json")"
    post_comment "$issue" "$comment_prefix <!-- claim-set:$value:$state:$generation -->" >/dev/null
    set_field "$issue" "claim=$value"
  elif [ "$(jq -r '.projection.write // false' "$scratch/held.json")" = true ]; then
    value="$(jq -r '.projection.desired' "$scratch/held.json")"
    if [ -n "$value" ]; then set_field "$issue" "claim=$value"; else clear_field "$issue" claim; fi
  fi
}

# 0 when the branch exists, 1 when GitHub says it does not, 2 when unknown.
ref_exists() {
  local err
  if pr_api "repos/$repo/git/ref/heads/$1" >/dev/null 2>"$scratch/ref-error"; then
    return 0
  fi
  err="$(cat "$scratch/ref-error")"
  case "$err" in
    *"Not Found"*|*"HTTP 404"*) return 1 ;;
  esac
  return 2
}

create_ref() {
  local ref="$1" sha="$2" default_branch="$3" url
  if pr_api --method POST "repos/$repo/git/refs" -f "ref=refs/heads/$ref" -f "sha=$sha" \
       >/dev/null 2>"$scratch/ref-error"; then
    return 0
  fi
  case "$(cat "$scratch/ref-error")" in
    *"HTTP 422"*) return 1 ;;
  esac
  # Claude Code cloud's proxy refuses this REST write but lets git push through.
  url="$(git remote get-url origin 2>/dev/null || true)"
  url="${url%/}"; url="${url%.git}"
  case "$url" in
    */"$repo"|*:"$repo") ;;
    *) printf 'and the current directory is not a checkout of %s to push from\n' "$repo" >>"$scratch/ref-error"
       return 2 ;;
  esac
  git cat-file -e "$sha^{commit}" 2>/dev/null \
    || git fetch --quiet origin "refs/heads/$default_branch" 2>>"$scratch/ref-error" || true
  if ! git cat-file -e "$sha^{commit}" 2>/dev/null; then
    printf 'and %s is not in this checkout to push\n' "$sha" >>"$scratch/ref-error"
    return 2
  fi
  if git push --porcelain --force-with-lease="refs/heads/$ref:" origin "$sha:refs/heads/$ref" \
       >"$scratch/push-out" 2>>"$scratch/ref-error"; then
    grep -q '^\*' "$scratch/push-out" && return 0
    cat "$scratch/push-out" >>"$scratch/ref-error"
    return 1
  fi
  cat "$scratch/push-out" >>"$scratch/ref-error"
  grep -q '^!.*stale info' "$scratch/push-out" && return 1
  return 2
}

claim_result() {
  local out="$1" outcome="$2" reason="$3"
  jq -n --argjson issue "$issue" --arg outcome "$outcome" --arg reason "$reason" \
    --arg state "$held" --arg ref "${ref:-}" --arg generation "${generation:-}" \
    --slurpfile settled <(cat "$scratch/settled.json" 2>/dev/null || printf 'null') \
    --slurpfile replay <(cat "$scratch/held.json" 2>/dev/null || cat "$scratch/unheld.json" 2>/dev/null || printf 'null') '
    {format: "task-queue-claim-v1", issue: $issue, outcome: $outcome,
     reason: (if $reason == "" then null else $reason end),
     state: $state,
     generation: (if $generation == "" then null else $generation end),
     ref: (if $ref == "" then null else $ref end),
     settlement: ($settled[0] // null), replay: ($replay[0] // null)}' >"$out"
}

cmd_claim() {
  local session="" session_given=0 review=0 resume=0 out_given="" unheld held kind
  issue=""; profile=""
  while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
    case "$1" in
      --profile) [ $# -ge 2 ] || die "--profile needs a value"; profile="$2"; shift 2 ;;
      --session)
        [ $# -ge 2 ] || die "--session needs a value"
        [ "$session_given" = 0 ] || die "session may be provided only once"
        session="$2"; session_given=1; shift 2
        ;;
      --review) review=1; shift ;;
      --resume) resume=1; shift ;;
      --out) [ $# -ge 2 ] || die "--out needs a value"; out_given="$2"; shift 2 ;;
      -h|--help) usage; exit 0 ;;
      -*) die "unknown flag: $1" ;;
      *) [ -z "$issue" ] || die "unexpected argument: $1"; issue="$1"; shift ;;
    esac
  done
  case "$issue" in ""|*[!0-9]*|0*) die "claim needs a positive issue number" ;; esac
  [ "$session_given" = 1 ] || die "claim needs --session"
  require_session_token "$session" "--session"
  if [ "$review" = 1 ]; then
    unheld="Needs review"; held="Under review"; kind=review
  else
    unheld="Ready"; held="In progress"; kind=issue
  fi
  gh_setup "$profile"
  local out fields live projection
  out="$(out_file "claim-$issue" "$out_given")"
  generation=""; ref=""

  fields="$(read_fields "$issue")"
  live="$(canon_queue "$(jq -r '.queue // ""' <<<"$fields")")"
  projection="$(jq -r '.claim // ""' <<<"$fields")"
  if [ "$resume" = 1 ]; then
    if [ "$live" != "$held" ]; then
      claim_result "$out" not-claimable "Queue is ${live:-unset}, not $held"
      printf 'not claimable #%s: Queue is %s, not %s; details %s\n' "$issue" "${live:-unset}" "$held" "$out"
      exit 3
    fi
    replay_issue "$issue" "$held" "$projection" "$scratch/held.json" \
      || die "claim replay of #$issue failed: $(replay_error)"
    if ! jq -e --arg s "$session" --arg state "$held" '
         .claim.value == $s and .claim.state == $state
         and .generation.id != null and .claim.generation == .generation.id' \
         "$scratch/held.json" >/dev/null; then
      claim_result "$out" not-claimable "not held by $session in its active generation"
      printf 'not claimable #%s: not held by %s in its active generation; details %s\n' "$issue" "$session" "$out"
      exit 3
    fi
    generation="$(jq -r '.generation.id' "$scratch/held.json")"
    ref="claude/$kind-$issue-$generation"
  else
    if [ "$live" != "$unheld" ]; then
      claim_result "$out" not-claimable "Queue is ${live:-unset}, not $unheld"
      printf 'not claimable #%s: Queue is %s, not %s; details %s\n' "$issue" "${live:-unset}" "$unheld" "$out"
      exit 3
    fi
    replay_issue "$issue" "$unheld" "$projection" "$scratch/unheld.json" \
      || die "claim replay of #$issue failed: $(replay_error)"
    if [ "$(jq -r '.transition.claimable' "$scratch/unheld.json")" != true ]; then
      local why
      why="$(jq -r '.transition | "\(.status): \(.reason // "not claimable")"' "$scratch/unheld.json")"
      claim_result "$out" not-claimable "$why"
      printf 'not claimable #%s: %s; details %s\n' "$issue" "$why" "$out"
      exit 3
    fi
    generation="$(jq -r '.generation.id' "$scratch/unheld.json")"
    ref="claude/$kind-$issue-$generation"

    # The marker goes first: a claimant that dies here leaves a marker the stale
    # half of the tie-break can clear, never a held state with no clock.
    post_comment "$issue" "$comment_prefix <!-- claim:$session:$held:$generation -->" >/dev/null
    set_field "$issue" "queue=$held"
    post_comment "$issue" "$comment_prefix <!-- claim-set:$session:$held:$generation -->" >/dev/null
    set_field "$issue" "claim=$session"
  fi

  local attempt=1 winner sha default_branch rc
  while :; do
    settle_fresh "$issue" "$held" "$session"
    winner="$(jq -r '.winner' "$scratch/settled.json")"
    if [ "$(jq -r '.outcome' "$scratch/settled.json")" != won ]; then
      ref=""
      claim_result "$out" lost "settlement names $winner"
      printf 'lost #%s to %s; Claim converged, Queue left %s; details %s\n' "$issue" "$winner" "$held" "$out"
      exit 3
    fi
    if [ "$attempt" -gt 1 ]; then
      rc=0; ref_exists "$ref" || rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" = 0 ]; then
        claim_result "$out" disagreement "settlement names this session but $ref already exists"
        die "settlement names this session but $ref already exists; do not work or review, and monitor until a fresh read agrees (details $out)"
      elif [ "$rc" = 2 ]; then
        die "cannot tell whether $ref exists: $(tr '\n' ' ' <"$scratch/ref-error")"
      fi
    fi
    if [ -z "${sha:-}" ]; then
      default_branch="$(pr_api "repos/$repo" | jq -er '.default_branch')" \
        || die "cannot read the default branch of $repo"
      sha="$(pr_api "repos/$repo/git/ref/heads/$default_branch" | jq -er '.object.sha')" \
        || die "cannot read the head of $default_branch"
    fi
    rc=0; create_ref "$ref" "$sha" "$default_branch" || rc=$?
    [ "$rc" = 0 ] && break
    if [ "$rc" = 2 ] || [ "$attempt" -ge 3 ]; then
      local reason
      reason="$(tr '\n' ' ' <"$scratch/ref-error" | sed 's/ *$//')"
      [ "$rc" = 2 ] || reason="rejected $attempt times: $reason"
      claim_result "$out" held-without-ref "$reason"
      printf 'holding #%s %s generation %s without ref %s: %s; retry with claim --resume or report the held claim; details %s\n' \
        "$issue" "$held" "$generation" "$ref" "$reason" "$out"
      exit 4
    fi
    attempt=$((attempt + 1))
  done
  claim_result "$out" won ""
  printf 'won #%s %s generation %s, ref %s; details %s\n' "$issue" "$held" "$generation" "$ref" "$out"
}

# --- handoff ------------------------------------------------------------------
cmd_handoff() {
  local session="" session_given=0 note_file="" touches="" touches_given=0 out_given="" prs=()
  issue=""; profile=""
  while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
    case "$1" in
      --profile) [ $# -ge 2 ] || die "--profile needs a value"; profile="$2"; shift 2 ;;
      --session)
        [ $# -ge 2 ] || die "--session needs a value"
        [ "$session_given" = 0 ] || die "session may be provided only once"
        session="$2"; session_given=1; shift 2
        ;;
      --pr)
        [ $# -ge 2 ] || die "--pr needs a value"
        case "$2" in ""|*[!0-9]*|0*) die "--pr needs a positive pull request number" ;; esac
        prs+=("$2"); shift 2
        ;;
      --note-file) [ $# -ge 2 ] || die "--note-file needs a value"; note_file="$2"; shift 2 ;;
      --touches) [ $# -ge 2 ] || die "--touches needs a value"; touches="$2"; touches_given=1; shift 2 ;;
      --out) [ $# -ge 2 ] || die "--out needs a value"; out_given="$2"; shift 2 ;;
      -h|--help) usage; exit 0 ;;
      -*) die "unknown flag: $1" ;;
      *) [ -z "$issue" ] || die "unexpected argument: $1"; issue="$1"; shift ;;
    esac
  done
  case "$issue" in ""|*[!0-9]*|0*) die "handoff needs a positive issue number" ;; esac
  [ "${#prs[@]}" -gt 0 ] || die "handoff needs at least one --pr"
  [ "$session_given" = 1 ] || die "handoff needs --session"
  require_session_token "$session" "--session"
  [ -n "$note_file" ] || die "handoff needs --note-file"
  [ -r "$note_file" ] || die "cannot read $note_file"
  local note
  note="$(cat "$note_file")"
  [ -n "${note//[[:space:]]/}" ] || die "the handoff note is empty"
  case "$note" in
    *"<!-- claim"*) die "the handoff note must not contain a claim protocol marker" ;;
  esac
  gh_setup "$profile"
  local out fields live projection generation pr unlinked
  out="$(out_file "handoff-$issue" "$out_given")"

  fields="$(read_fields "$issue")"
  live="$(canon_queue "$(jq -r '.queue // ""' <<<"$fields")")"
  [ "$live" = "In progress" ] || die "#$issue is ${live:-unset}, not In progress"
  projection="$(jq -r '.claim // ""' <<<"$fields")"
  replay_issue "$issue" "In progress" "$projection" "$scratch/held.json" \
    || die "claim replay of #$issue failed: $(replay_error)"
  jq -e --arg s "$session" '
    .claim.value == $s and .claim.state == "In progress"
    and .generation.id != null and .claim.generation == .generation.id' \
    "$scratch/held.json" >/dev/null \
    || die "#$issue is not held by $session in its active generation; stop writing"
  generation="$(jq -r '.generation.id' "$scratch/held.json")"

  : >"$scratch/prs.jsonl"
  for pr in "${prs[@]}"; do
    pr_api "repos/$repo/pulls/$pr" >"$scratch/pr.json" || die "cannot read PR #$pr"
    jq -e '.state == "open"' "$scratch/pr.json" >/dev/null || die "PR #$pr is not open"
    jq -c "$pr_owners_jq"' {number, head: (.head.ref // ""), base: (.base.ref // ""), owners: owners}' \
      "$scratch/pr.json" >>"$scratch/prs.jsonl"
  done
  unlinked="$(jq -rs --argjson n "$issue" '
    def stacked($a; $b): ($a.head != "" and $a.head == $b.base) or ($b.head != "" and $b.head == $a.base);
    . as $prs
    | reduce range(length) as $_ ([$prs[] | select(.owners | index($n)) | .number];
        . as $ok
        | . + [$prs[] | select(. as $p | ($ok | index($p.number) | not)
                                and any($prs[] | select(.number as $m | $ok | index($m)); stacked($p; .)))
                      | .number]
        | unique)
    | . as $ok | [$prs[] | select(.number as $m | $ok | index($m) | not) | .number] | .[0] // empty' \
    "$scratch/prs.jsonl")"
  [ -z "$unlinked" ] \
    || die "PR #$unlinked does not name #$issue by a closing reference or claude/ branch, and is not stacked on or under a PR that does"

  if [ "$touches_given" = 1 ]; then
    touches="$(printf '%s' "$touches" | tr -s '[:space:]' ' ' | sed 's/^ //; s/ $//')"
    if [ -n "$touches" ]; then set_field "$issue" "touches=$touches"; else clear_field "$issue" touches; fi
  fi

  case "$note" in
    "[Agent] "*|"[Cursor] "*|"$comment_prefix "*) ;;
    *) note="$comment_prefix $note" ;;
  esac
  post_comment "$issue" "$note" >/dev/null
  post_comment "$issue" "$comment_prefix <!-- claim-clear:In progress:$generation -->" >/dev/null
  local intent
  intent="$(post_comment "$issue" "$comment_prefix <!-- claim-cycle:Needs review:$generation -->")"
  set_field "$issue" "queue=Needs review"
  post_comment "$issue" "$comment_prefix <!-- claim-cycle-activate:$intent -->" >/dev/null
  clear_field "$issue" claim

  fields="$(read_fields "$issue")"
  live="$(canon_queue "$(jq -r '.queue // ""' <<<"$fields")")"
  projection="$(jq -r '.claim // ""' <<<"$fields")"
  replay_issue "$issue" "${live:-Triage}" "$projection" "$scratch/after.json" \
    || die "verification replay of #$issue failed: $(replay_error)"
  jq -n --argjson issue "$issue" --arg live "$live" --arg intent "$intent" \
    --arg previous "$generation" --argjson prs "$(printf '%s\n' "${prs[@]}" | jq -s 'map(tonumber)')" \
    --slurpfile r "$scratch/after.json" '
    ($r[0]) as $r
    | {format: "task-queue-handoff-v1", issue: $issue, pull_requests: $prs,
       queue: $live, previous_generation: $previous, intent: $intent,
       generation: ($r.generation.id // null),
       verified: ($live == "Needs review" and $r.transition.claimable == true
                  and $r.claim == null and (($r.projection.write // false) | not)),
       replay: $r}' >"$out"
  if [ "$(jq -r '.verified' "$out")" != true ]; then
    die "handoff of #$issue did not verify (Queue ${live:-unset}, transition $(jq -c '.replay.transition' "$out")); details $out"
  fi
  printf 'handed off #%s to Needs review generation %s with PR %s; details %s\n' \
    "$issue" "$(jq -r '.generation' "$out")" \
    "$(printf '#%s ' "${prs[@]}" | sed 's/ $//; s/ /, /g')" "$out"
}

case "$cmd" in
  snapshot) { set +x; } 2>/dev/null; cmd_snapshot "$@"; exit 0 ;;
  claim)    { set +x; } 2>/dev/null; cmd_claim "$@"; exit 0 ;;
  handoff)  { set +x; } 2>/dev/null; cmd_handoff "$@"; exit 0 ;;
esac

if [ "$cmd" = settle ]; then
  scenario_file=""; as_json=0
  while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
    case "$1" in
      --scenario) [ $# -ge 2 ] || die "--scenario needs a value"; scenario_file="$2"; shift 2 ;;
      --json) as_json=1; shift ;;
      -h|--help) usage; exit 0 ;;
      -*) die "unknown flag: $1" ;;
      *) die "unexpected argument: $1" ;;
    esac
  done
  command -v jq >/dev/null 2>&1 || die "jq is required"
  [ -n "$scenario_file" ] || die "settle needs --scenario"
  [ -r "$scenario_file" ] || die "cannot read $scenario_file"
  scenario="$(cat "$scenario_file")"
  validate_unique_json "$scenario"

  settlement="$(printf '%s' "$scenario" | jq \
    --arg session_token_regex "$session_token_regex" '
    def session_token:
      if type == "string" then test($session_token_regex) else false end;
    def iso:
      try (
        (capture("^(?<whole>[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})(?:[.](?<fraction>[0-9]+))?(?<zone>Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})$") // null) as $p
        | if $p == null then null
          else
            ($p.whole + "Z" | fromdateiso8601) as $base
            | if ($base | strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")) != ($p.whole + "Z") then null
              elif $p.zone != "Z" and
                   (($p.zone[1:3] | tonumber) > 23 or
                    ($p.zone[4:6] | tonumber) > 59)
              then null
              else
                $base
                + (if $p.fraction == null then 0
                   else ("0." + $p.fraction | tonumber) end)
                + (if $p.zone == "Z" then 0
                   else
                     (($p.zone[1:3] | tonumber) * 3600
                      + ($p.zone[4:6] | tonumber) * 60)
                     * (if $p.zone[0:1] == "+" then -1 else 1 end)
                   end)
              end
          end
      ) catch null;
    . as $s
    | (if type != "object" then
        ["scenario must be an object"]
      else [
        (if (.issue | type) != "number" or .issue <= 0 or (.issue | floor) != .issue then "issue must be a positive integer" else empty end),
        (if (.caller | session_token | not) then "caller must be a session token" else empty end),
        (if (.target_state == "In progress" or .target_state == "Under review") | not then "target_state must be In progress or Under review" else empty end),
        (if .claim == null then empty
         elif (.claim | type) != "object" then
           "claim must be null or a scoped Claim event"
         elif ((.claim | keys | sort) != ["generation", "state", "value"] or
               (.claim.value | session_token | not) or
               (.claim.state != "In progress" and .claim.state != "Under review") or
               (.claim.generation | type) != "string" or
               (.claim.generation | test("^[0-9A-Za-z][0-9A-Za-z._-]*$") | not))
         then "claim value must be a session token with only held state and ref-safe generation"
         elif .claim.state != .target_state or .claim.generation != .generation then
           "claim must match the target state and active generation"
         else empty end),
        (if (.generation | type) != "string" or
            (.generation | test("^[0-9A-Za-z][0-9A-Za-z._-]*$") | not)
         then "generation must be a ref-safe nonblank string" else empty end),
        (if (.now | type) != "string" or (.now | iso) == null then "now must be an ISO-8601 timestamp" else empty end),
        (if (.stale_after_seconds | type) != "number" or .stale_after_seconds <= 0 then "stale_after_seconds must be positive" else empty end),
        (if (.markers | type) != "array" then "markers must be an array" else empty end),
        (if (.markers | type) == "array" and
            (.markers | all(
              type == "object" and
              (.session | session_token) and
              (.state == "In progress" or .state == "Under review") and
              (.generation | type) == "string" and
              (.generation | test("^[0-9A-Za-z][0-9A-Za-z._-]*$")) and
              (.created_at | type) == "string" and (.created_at | iso) != null and
              (.order | type) == "number" and .order > 0 and (.order | floor) == .order
            ) | not)
         then "every marker needs a session token, claim state, ref-safe generation, ISO created_at, and positive integer order" else empty end),
        (if (.markers | type) == "array" and
            (([.markers[].order] | unique | length) != (.markers | length))
         then "marker orders must be unique" else empty end),
        (if (.markers | type) == "array" and
            (.caller | type) == "string" and
            (.generation | type) == "string" and
            (.target_state == "In progress" or .target_state == "Under review") and
            ((.markers | any(.[];
                type == "object" and
                .session == $s.caller and
                .state == $s.target_state and
                .generation == $s.generation)) | not)
         then "markers must include the caller in the target state and generation" else empty end),
        (if (.markers | type) == "array" and
            (.claim | type) == "object" and
            (.claim.value | session_token) and
            .claim.state == .target_state and
            .claim.generation == .generation and
            ((.markers | any(.[];
                type == "object" and
                .session == $s.claim.value and
                .state == $s.claim.state and
                .generation == $s.claim.generation)) | not)
         then "Claim must have a marker in the target state and generation" else empty end)
      ] end) as $problems
    | if ($problems | length) > 0 then
        {error: ($problems | join("; "))}
      else
        (.now | iso) as $now
        | (if .claim == null then null else .claim.value end) as $claim
        | [.markers[]
           | select(.state == $s.target_state and .generation == $s.generation)
           | . + {epoch: (.created_at | iso)}
           | . + {stale: (($now - .epoch) > $s.stale_after_seconds)}
           | select((.stale and ($claim != .session)) | not)]
          | sort_by(.epoch, .order) as $survivors
        | if ($survivors | length) == 0 then
            {error: "no surviving marker for the target state"}
          else
            $survivors[0] as $winner
            | {
                winner: $winner.session,
                outcome: (if $s.caller == $winner.session then "won" else "lost" end),
                desired_claim: $winner.session,
                desired_claim_event: {
                  value: $winner.session,
                  state: $s.target_state,
                  generation: $s.generation
                },
                generation: $s.generation,
                write_claim: ($claim != $winner.session),
                queue_action: "leave",
                create_ref: ($s.caller == $winner.session),
                ref: (if $s.target_state == "In progress"
                      then "claude/issue-\($s.issue)-\($s.generation)"
                      else "claude/review-\($s.issue)-\($s.generation)" end),
                surviving_markers: ($survivors | length)
              }
          end
      end
  ' 2>/dev/null)" || die "invalid settlement scenario"

  error="$(printf '%s' "$settlement" | jq -r '.error // empty')"
  [ -z "$error" ] || die "$error"
  if [ "$as_json" = 1 ]; then
    printf '%s\n' "$settlement"
  else
    printf '%s' "$settlement" | jq -r \
      '"winner: \(.winner)\noutcome: \(.outcome)\ndesired Claim: \(.desired_claim)\nref: \(.ref)"'
  fi
  exit 0
fi

target=""; issues_file="${TASK_QUEUE_ISSUES_FILE:-}"; as_json=0
selection_queue="Ready"; selection_queue_given=0
prefer=0; prefer_given=0
reviewer=""; reviewer_given=0
runtime=""; runtime_given=0
while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
  case "$1" in
    --issues) [ $# -ge 2 ] || die "--issues needs a value"; issues_file="$2"; shift 2 ;;
    --queue) [ $# -ge 2 ] || die "--queue needs a value"; selection_queue="$2"; selection_queue_given=1; shift 2 ;;
    --reviewer)
      [ $# -ge 2 ] || die "--reviewer needs a value"
      [ "$reviewer_given" = 0 ] || die "reviewer may be provided only once"
      reviewer="$2"; reviewer_given=1; shift 2
      ;;
    --runtime)
      [ $# -ge 2 ] || die "--runtime needs a value"
      [ "$runtime_given" = 0 ] || die "runtime may be provided only once"
      runtime="$2"; runtime_given=1; shift 2
      ;;
    --prefer) [ $# -ge 2 ] || die "--prefer needs a value"; prefer="$2"; prefer_given=1; shift 2 ;;
    --json)   as_json=1; shift ;;
    -h|--help) usage; exit 0 ;;
    -*)       die "unknown flag: $1" ;;
    *)        if [ -n "$target" ]; then die "unexpected argument: $1"; fi; target="$1"; shift ;;
  esac
done

if [ "$selection_queue_given" = 1 ] && [ "$cmd" != "next" ]; then
  die "--queue is only valid with next"
fi
if [ "$prefer_given" = 1 ] && [ "$cmd" != "next" ]; then
  die "--prefer is only valid with next"
fi
if [ "$reviewer_given" = 1 ] &&
   { [ "$cmd" != "next" ] || [ "$selection_queue" != "Needs review" ]; }; then
  die '--reviewer is only valid with --queue "Needs review"'
fi
if [ "$runtime_given" = 1 ] &&
   { [ "$cmd" != "next" ] || [ "$selection_queue" != "Needs review" ]; }; then
  die '--runtime is only valid with --queue "Needs review"'
fi
case "$selection_queue" in
  Ready|"Needs review") ;;
  *) die "supported selection states are Ready and Needs review" ;;
esac
if [ "$cmd" = "next" ] && [ "$selection_queue" = "Needs review" ]; then
  [ "$reviewer_given" = 1 ] \
    || die '--reviewer is required with --queue "Needs review"'
  require_session_token "$reviewer" "reviewer"
  [ "$runtime_given" = 1 ] \
    || die '--runtime is required with --queue "Needs review"'
  case "$runtime" in
    cloud|local) ;;
    *) die "--runtime must be cloud or local" ;;
  esac
fi
if [ "$prefer_given" = 1 ]; then
  case "$prefer" in
    ""|*[!0-9]*|0) die "--prefer needs a positive issue number" ;;
  esac
  [ "$selection_queue" = "Needs review" ] \
    || die "--prefer is only valid with --queue \"Needs review\""
fi

if [ "$cmd" = "why" ]; then
  [ -n "$target" ] || die "why needs an issue number"
  case "$target" in (*[!0-9]*) die "not an issue number: $target" ;; esac
  [ "$target" -gt 0 ] || die "not an issue number: $target"
fi

# next reshapes its whole output around a positional it never asked for, which
# turns `next 2` into `why 2` silently -- and a --json caller reading .next then
# sees null and concludes nothing is pickable.
if [ "$cmd" = "next" ] && [ -n "$target" ]; then
  die "next takes no issue number (did you mean: why $target?)"
fi

command -v jq >/dev/null 2>&1 || die "jq is required"

if [ -n "$issues_file" ]; then
  [ -r "$issues_file" ] || die "cannot read $issues_file"
  input="$(cat "$issues_file")"
else
  [ ! -t 0 ] || die "no input: pass --issues, set TASK_QUEUE_ISSUES_FILE, or pipe JSON on stdin"
  input="$(cat)"
fi

validate_unique_json "$input"
printf '%s' "$input" | jq -e 'type == "array"' >/dev/null 2>&1 \
  || die "input is not a JSON array"
printf '%s' "$input" | jq -e 'all(type == "object")' >/dev/null 2>&1 \
  || die "every entry in the input must be an issue object"

# Only the JSON shape is refused here, and only a normaliser can get that wrong
# -- it decides every type in this document. What a person typed into a text
# field is content, and content is reported per issue instead, because refusing
# the board over it stops every agent in the fleet: "#134 96" under Blocked by
# issue is one human being ordinary, and it used to fail this gate.
problems="$(printf '%s' "$input" | jq -r \
  --arg session_token_regex "$session_token_regex" '
  def session_token:
    if type == "string" then test($session_token_regex) else false end;
  def ref: "#\(.number // "?")";
  [ .[]
    | (if (.number | type) != "number"
       then "every issue needs a numeric number" else empty end),
      (if .queue != null and (.queue | type) != "string"
       then "\(ref): queue must be a string" else empty end),
      (if .priority != null and (.priority | type) != "string"
       then "\(ref): priority must be a string" else empty end),
      (if .claim != null and (.claim | type) != "string"
       then "\(ref): claim must be a string" else empty end),
      (if .context_only != null and (.context_only | type) != "boolean"
       then "\(ref): context_only must be a boolean" else empty end),
      (if .normalization_error != null
          and ((.normalization_error | type) != "string"
               or (.normalization_error | test("\\S") | not))
       then "\(ref): normalization_error must be a nonempty string" else empty end),
      (if has("implementation_authors") then
         if ((.implementation_authors | type) != "array"
             or (.implementation_authors | length) == 0
             or (.implementation_authors
                 | map(session_token | not)
                 | any)
             or ((.implementation_authors | unique | length)
                 != (.implementation_authors | length)))
         then "\(ref): implementation_authors must be a nonempty array of unique session tokens"
         else empty end
       else empty end),
      (if has("runtime_target")
          and (.runtime_target != null)
          and (.runtime_target as $t | ["cloud", "local", "either", "both"] | any(. == $t) | not)
       then "\(ref): runtime_target must be cloud, local, either, both, or null"
       else empty end),
      (if .touches != null and ((.touches | type) != "array"
                                or (.touches | map(type != "string") | any))
       then "\(ref): touches must be an array of paths" else empty end),
      (if .blocked_by != null
          and ((.blocked_by | type) != "array"
               or (.blocked_by | map((type == "number") or (type == "string") | not) | any))
       then "\(ref): blocked_by must be an array of issue numbers or text" else empty end),
      (if .stack_ancestors == null then empty
       elif (.stack_ancestors | type) != "array"
         or (.stack_ancestors
             | any((type != "number") or . <= 0 or (floor != .)))
         or ((.stack_ancestors | unique | length) != (.stack_ancestors | length))
       then "\(ref): stack_ancestors must be an array of unique positive issue numbers"
       else empty end),
      (if .open_prs == null then empty
       elif (.open_prs | type) != "array"
         or (.open_prs
             | any((type != "number") or . <= 0 or (floor != .)))
         or ((.open_prs | unique | length) != (.open_prs | length))
       then "\(ref): open_prs must be an array of unique positive pull request numbers"
       else empty end)
  ]
  + ([.[].number | select(type == "number")] | group_by(.)
     | map(select(length > 1) | "#\(.[0]) appears more than once in the input"))
  | unique | .[]')"
if [ -n "$problems" ]; then
  printf '%s\n' "$problems" | while IFS= read -r p; do
    echo "task-queue: $p" >&2
  done
  exit 1
fi

cycles="$(printf '%s' "$input" | jq -r '
  . as $issues
  | def parents($number):
      [$issues[]
       | select(.number == $number)
       | (.stack_ancestors // [])[]];
    def reaches($number; $target; $seen):
      if ($seen | index($number)) != null then false
      else any(parents($number)[];
        . == $target or reaches(.; $target; $seen + [$number]))
      end;
  [.[] | select(reaches(.number; .number; [])) | .number]
  | unique
  | if length == 0 then empty
    else "stack ancestry contains a cycle involving "
         + (map("#\(.)") | join(", "))
    end
')"
if [ -n "$cycles" ]; then
  die "$cycles"
fi

verdict="$(printf '%s' "$input" | jq --argjson want "${target:-0}" \
  --arg select_state "$selection_queue" --arg reviewer "$reviewer" \
  --arg runtime "$runtime" \
  --argjson prefer "$prefer" '
  # A touches entry is a path or a directory glob. Strip the glob tail so the
  # comparison is a path-prefix one, then require the prefix to land on a
  # segment boundary -- without that, "a/b" would swallow "a/bc".
  #
  # Brace expansion is NOT handled: "rules/{a,b}.mjs" is read as one literal
  # path that matches nothing. List the files separately.
  # A leading "/" or "./" is what somebody writes when asked for a path in a
  # repo, so strip those too -- "/src/app.ts" and "src/app.ts" naming different
  # files was a lock that silently missed. Every spelling of "the whole repo"
  # reduces to nothing, and an entry that reduces to nothing is reported rather
  # than left to look like a lock.
  def trim: sub("^\\s+"; "") | sub("\\s+$"; "");
  def norm:
    trim
    | sub("^\\./"; "")
    | sub("/\\*\\*$"; "") | sub("/\\*$"; "")
    | sub("^\\*\\*$"; "")  | sub("^\\*$"; "") | sub("^\\.$"; "")
    | sub("/+$"; "") | sub("^/+"; "");
  def overlaps($a; $b):
    any($a[]; . as $x | any($b[]; . as $y |
      ($x == $y)
      or (($y + "/") | startswith($x + "/"))
      or (($x + "/") | startswith($y + "/"))));

  # Priority is a named option rather than a number, so the order it implies has
  # to be written down. Unlike an integer rank this cannot drift quietly: an
  # option outside the table sorts last AND says so.
  {"urgent": 0, "high": 1, "medium": 2, "low": 3} as $rank_of
  | 9 as $unranked
  | ["In progress", "Needs review", "Under review", "Ready to merge"] as $inflight
  # The seven are listed again rather than built from $inflight. Deriving them
  # made dropping a state from $inflight turn it unknown, which holds files for
  # the other reason -- so the suite stayed green under the one mutation that
  # matters most here. Two separate facts, two separate lists.
  | ["Triage", "Waiting for input", "Ready", "In progress", "Needs review", "Under review", "Ready to merge"] as $states
  | ($states | map({key: ascii_downcase, value: .}) | from_entries) as $queue_of
  # Blanks are dropped AFTER norm, not before: norm turns "/" and "/**" into ""
  # just as surely as a double space does, and an empty entry equals the other
  # empty entry on the other issue, so two tasks collide over nothing at all.
  #
  # An unset single-select reaches us as "" as readily as as an absent key, and
  # the two must not mean opposite things now that an unrecognised state holds
  # every file it names.
  # Every number in an entry, not the first: reading only the first silently
  # dropped the rest, so an unsplit "134 96" was handed out as blocked by #134
  # alone and its real blocker went unreported. An entry carrying more than one
  # number, or whitespace after trimming, is a caller that did not split -- the
  # likeliest normalisation bug here, since the field itself holds "134 96".
  | map(. + {
      _touches:    ((.touches // []) | map(norm) | map(select(test("\\S")))),
      _empty_touches: ((.touches // []) | map(select(norm | test("\\S") | not))),
      _unsplit_touches: ((.touches // []) | map(trim) | map(select(test("\\s")))),
      _glob_touches: ((.touches // []) | map(select(norm | test("\\*")))),
      _blocked_by: ((.blocked_by // [])
                    | map(if type == "string" then [scan("[0-9]+") | tonumber] else [.] end)
                    | flatten),
      _stack_ancestry_present: has("stack_ancestors"),
      _stack_ancestors: (.stack_ancestors // []),
      _open_prs: (.open_prs // []),
      _implementation_authors_present: has("implementation_authors"),
      _implementation_authors: (.implementation_authors // []),
      _review_fields_present: has("implementation_authors"),
      _runtime_target_present: has("runtime_target"),
      _runtime_target: (.runtime_target // null),
      _unreadable_blockers: ((.blocked_by // [])
                             | map(select(type == "string" and test("\\S")
                                          and ([scan("[0-9]+")] | length) == 0))),
      _unsplit_blockers: ((.blocked_by // [])
                          | map(select(type == "string"
                                       and (((trim | test("\\s")) or ([scan("[0-9]+")] | length) > 1))))),
      _priority:   (.priority // null),
      _claim:      (if ((.claim // "") | test("^\\s*$")) then null else (.claim | trim) end),
      _context_only: (.context_only // false),
      _normalization_error: (.normalization_error // null),
      _queue:      (if ((.queue // "") | test("^\\s*$")) then "Triage" else .queue end)
    })
  | map(. + {
      _canon_queue: ($queue_of[._queue | ascii_downcase] // null),
      _runtime_compatible: (._runtime_target == null or ._runtime_target == "either"
                            or ._runtime_target == $runtime),
      _review_excluded: ($reviewer as $identity | (._implementation_authors | index($identity)) != null)
    })
  | map(. + {
      _order: (if ._priority == null then $unranked
               else ($rank_of[._priority | ascii_downcase] // $unranked) end),
      _unknown_priority: (._priority != null
                          and ($rank_of[._priority | ascii_downcase] == null)),
      _ready_with_pr: (._canon_queue == "Ready" and (._open_prs | length) > 0),
      _holds_files: (._canon_queue as $q
                     | $q == null or ($inflight | index($q)) != null)
    })
  | . as $all
  | ([$all[].number]) as $present
  | map(
      . as $i
      # The input is every open issue, so "present" is exactly "still open" and
      # "absent" is exactly "closed". No second lookup can say more than that.
      | ($i._blocked_by | map(select(. as $n | $present | index($n)))) as $still_open
      | ($i._blocked_by - $still_open) as $absent
      | ($i._stack_ancestors | map(select(. as $n | $present | index($n)))) as $stack_ancestors_open
      | ($all
         | map(select(.number != $i.number
                      and ((overlaps($i._touches; ._touches)
                            and (._holds_files
                                 or ($select_state == "Ready" and ._ready_with_pr and ($i._ready_with_pr | not))))
                           or ($select_state == "Ready" and ._holds_files
                               and any(._open_prs[]; . as $p | $i._open_prs | index($p) != null)))))
         | (if $select_state == "Needs review"
            then map(select(._canon_queue != "Needs review" or ._normalization_error != null)) # a waiting review holds nothing against another review
            else .
            end)
         | map(.number)) as $collisions
      | {
          number:   $i.number,
          title:    ($i.title // ""),
          # The field as it reads, and the canonical reading of it. Reporting
          # only the reading hid an unset field behind the Triage it stands in
          # for, and left every consumer to redo the case-insensitive match --
          # the one query SKILL.md asks a reviewer for, selecting on Needs
          # review, missed an issue whose field was typed in the wrong case.
          queue:    ($i.queue // null),
          state:    $i._canon_queue,
          claim:    $i._claim,
          context_only: $i._context_only,
          normalization_error: $i._normalization_error,
          open_prs: (if $i | has("open_prs") then $i._open_prs else null end),
          implementation_authors:
            (if $i._implementation_authors_present
             then $i._implementation_authors else null end),
          review_excluded:
            (if $i._implementation_authors_present
             then $i._review_excluded else null end),
          runtime_target: $i._runtime_target,
          runtime_compatible:
            (if $select_state == "Needs review" and $i._runtime_target_present
             then $i._runtime_compatible else null end),
          priority: $i._priority,
          order:    $i._order,
          eligible: (($i._context_only | not) and ($i._normalization_error == null)
                     and ($i._canon_queue == $select_state) and ($still_open | length) == 0
                     and ($select_state != "Needs review" or $i._stack_ancestry_present)
                     and ($select_state != "Needs review" or ($i._review_fields_present and ($i._review_excluded | not)))
                     and ($select_state != "Needs review" or ($i._runtime_target_present and $i._runtime_compatible))
                     and ($stack_ancestors_open | length) == 0
                     and ($collisions | length) == 0 and ($i._unreadable_blockers | length) == 0
                     and ($i._unsplit_blockers | length) == 0),
          adopt_open_pr: ($select_state == "Ready" and $i._ready_with_pr),
          blocked_by_open: $still_open,
          stack_ancestors: $i._stack_ancestors,
          stack_ancestors_open: $stack_ancestors_open,
          collides_with:   $collisions,
          warnings: (($absent | map("#\($i.number) names blocked_by #\(.), which is not in the input; read as closed"))
                     + ($i._unreadable_blockers
                        | map("#\($i.number) has a Blocked by issue entry with no number in it (\"\(.)\"); held back until it is readable"))
                     + ($i._empty_touches
                        | map("#\($i.number) has a Touches entry that names no path (\"\(.)\"); it locks nothing"))
                     + ($i._unsplit_touches
                        | map("#\($i.number) has a Touches entry with a space in it (\"\(.)\"); it was not split, so it matches no path and locks nothing"))
                     + ($i._glob_touches
                        | map("#\($i.number) has a Touches entry with a * left in it (\"\(.)\"); only a trailing /* or /** is understood, so it locks nothing"))
                     + ($i._unsplit_blockers
                        | map("#\($i.number) has a Blocked by issue entry that was not split (\"\(.)\"); held back until each number is its own entry"))
                     # The two states an agent is meant to be holding, which is
                     # the precondition the reclaim rule uses. Needs review and
                     # Ready to merge are held by nobody, by design.
                     + (if (["In progress", "Under review"] | index($i._canon_queue)) != null and $i._claim == null
                        then ["#\($i.number) is \($i._queue) with no Claim, so it holds its files and nobody holds it"]
                        else [] end)
                     + (if $i._unknown_priority
                        then ["#\($i.number) has priority \"\($i._priority)\", which is not one of Urgent, High, Medium, Low; sorted last"]
                        else [] end)
                     + (if $i._ready_with_pr
                        then ["#\($i.number) is Ready but already has open PR \($i._open_prs | map("#\(.)") | join(", ")); adopt or verify that PR rather than implementing it again"]
                        else [] end)
                     + (if $i._canon_queue == null
                        then ["#\($i.number) has queue \"\($i._queue)\", which is not one of Triage, Waiting for input, Ready, In progress, Needs review, Under review, Ready to merge; its files stay held"]
                        else [] end)
                     + (if $i._canon_queue != null and $i._holds_files and ($i._touches | length) == 0
                        then ["#\($i.number) is \($i._queue) and declares no Touches, so it holds no files"]
                        else [] end))
        }
      | .reasons = (
          (if $i._context_only then ["context-only blocker, not project work"] else [] end)
          + (if $i._normalization_error != null
             then ["normalization failed: \($i._normalization_error)"] else [] end)
          + (if $i._canon_queue != $select_state then ["queue is \($i._queue), not \($select_state)"] else [] end)
          + (if $select_state == "Needs review" and ($i._stack_ancestry_present | not)
             then ["stack_ancestors is required for Needs review selection"] else [] end)
          + (if $select_state == "Needs review" and ($i._implementation_authors_present | not)
             then ["implementation_authors is required for Needs review selection"] else [] end)
          + (if $select_state == "Needs review" and $i._implementation_authors_present and $i._review_excluded
             then ["self-authored implementation is excluded from review"] else [] end)
          + (if $select_state == "Needs review" and ($i._runtime_target_present | not)
             then ["runtime_target is required for Needs review selection"] else [] end)
          + (if $select_state == "Needs review" and $i._runtime_target_present and ($i._runtime_compatible | not)
             then [if $i._runtime_target == "both"
                   then "runtime target both needs cloud and local checks, which one \($runtime) reviewer cannot cover"
                   else "runtime target \($i._runtime_target) needs a \($i._runtime_target) reviewer, not \($runtime)" end]
             else [] end)
          + (.blocked_by_open | map("blocked by #\(.), still open"))
          + (.stack_ancestors_open | map("waiting for stack ancestor #\(.), still open"))
          + (if $select_state == "Ready" and $i._ready_with_pr
             then ["adopt or verify open PR \($i._open_prs | map("#\(.)") | join(", ")) rather than implementing again"]
             else [] end)
          + (.collides_with
             | map(. as $n
                   | ($all[] | select(.number == $n)) as $holder
                   | ($holder._open_prs | map(. as $p | select($i._open_prs | index($p) != null))) as $shared
                   | if $select_state == "Ready" and $holder._holds_files and ($shared | length) > 0
                     then "shares open PR \($shared | map("#\(.)") | join(", ")) with #\($n), in flight"
                     elif $holder._holds_files then "touches code held by #\($n), in flight"
                     else "touches code held by #\($n), which has unmerged open PR \($holder._open_prs | map("#\(.)") | join(", "))" end))
          + ($i._unreadable_blockers | map("blocked by \"\(.)\", which names no issue number"))
          + ($i._unsplit_blockers | map("blocked by \"\(.)\", which was not split into one number per entry"))
        )
    )
  | sort_by((if .eligible then 0 else 1 end), (if .adopt_open_pr then 1 else 0 end), .order, .number) as $canonical
  | (($canonical | map(select(.number == $prefer and .eligible)) | first | .number) // null) as $preferred
  | (if $preferred == null then $canonical
     else [$canonical[] | select(.number == $preferred)]
          + [$canonical[] | select(.number != $preferred)]
     end) as $ordered
  | { queue: $ordered,
      next: ($preferred // ($canonical | map(select(.eligible)) | first | .number // null)) }
  | if $want > 0 then { asked: $want, issue: (.queue[] | select(.number == $want)) } else . end
')"

# Before the --json branch, not inside the text one: an empty selection makes
# the whole verdict empty, so --json used to print nothing and exit 0 -- and
# --json is the path a caller scripts against.
if [ "$cmd" = "why" ]; then
  printf '%s' "$verdict" | jq -e '.issue' >/dev/null 2>&1 \
    || die "#$target is not in the input (closed, or not fetched)"
fi

if [ "$as_json" = 1 ]; then
  printf '%s\n' "$verdict"
  exit 0
fi

if [ "$cmd" = "why" ]; then
  printf '%s' "$verdict" | jq -r '
    .issue
    | "#\(.number)  \(.title)",
      "queue:    \(.state)    priority: \(.priority // "unset")",
      (if .eligible then "verdict:  pickable" else "verdict:  not pickable" end),
      (.reasons   | map("  - " + .) | .[]),
      (.warnings  | map("  ! " + .) | .[])'
  exit 0
fi

printf '%s' "$verdict" | jq -r '
  (.queue | map(select(.eligible))
   | if length == 0 then "nothing is pickable right now"
     else "pickable, in order:", (.[] | "  \(.priority // "--")  #\(.number)  \(.title)") end),
  (.queue | map(select(.eligible | not))
   | if length == 0 then empty
     else "", "held back:",
          (.[] | "  \(.priority // "--")  #\(.number)  \(.title)\n      \(.reasons | join("; "))")
     end),
  (.queue | map(.warnings) | add // [] | unique
   | if length == 0 then empty else "", (.[] | "  ! " + .) end)'
